            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of an accessory hepatic lobe in a child: ultrasound, computed tomographic, and magnetic resonance imaging findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>526-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of acute epigastric pain resulting from torsion of an accessory hepatic lobe is reported. Sonographic, computerized tomographic, and magnetic resonance findings are illustrated and the surgical management is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
